{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said to Noah, Come, etc., for you I have seen.</b> One needs to know why it was necessary to introduce this reason anew?" "<b>It appears</b> that HaShem was concerned for Noah lest he err in the meaning of HaShem's words when He said <b>Come, you and all your household, into the ark</b>, in one of two ways: either he might think that they are all righteous and therefore were saved on their own merit — and for this reason the difficulty we raised on the verse (Genesis 6:14) ״עֲשֵׂה לְךָ״ is hard. Or he might think that his sons and his sons' wives were saved only because they had not yet reached the category of punishment, and from this Noah might think to bring in and save the young children of the generation — his relatives and acquaintances — judging in his own mind that they are not liable to punishment. And even if he would not do so, at any rate it would be a foreign matter in his mind: why should those who are not subject to punishment not be saved? Therefore HaShem said to him <b>for you</b>, etc., giving a reason for His saying ״and all your household״ — not because they were worthy, and not because they had not yet reached the age of punishment, but rather on account of your merit, <b>for you I have seen</b>, etc. And from now on, anyone whose father is not righteous will be caught in the snare. And here He informed him that all who had not reached the category of punishment were nevertheless punished for the sin of their fathers — ״the fathers shall die without children״ (all the fathers), but not so Noah." "<b>Further,</b> it may be explained according to what they say in the Talmud (Sanhedrin 110a): Minor children of Israel have a share in the world to come, but minor children of the nations of the world do not have a share in the world to come. And in the generation of the Flood, all of them have the status of the nations of the world — for even though they had not reached the age of punishment, they are judged with the same judgment as the wicked, for <b>the deeds of the fathers, the children will do</b>; seed of evildoers, children who deal corruptly. But Noah was judged by the standard of minor children of Israel, and they were saved on account of their father's merit — even when wrath comes upon the world, HaShem protects them."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:40:00.625483930Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}